r TMB variation: H2O2 fixed at 20 mM. \n     - For H2O2 variation: TMB fixed at 320 μM = 0.32 mM. \n   - **Dimensions**: 'diameters of 4–25 nm', 'average size was about 12 nm'. Since they are spherical dots, length/width/depth can be 12 nm. \n   - **Formula**: Si. \n   - **Syngony**: 'single crystalline structures'. XRD/ED patterns indicate crystalline. Silicon is typically cubic (diamond cubic). The text doesn't explicitly name the crystal system (e.g., 'cubic'), just 'single crystalline'. I will leave syngony as null unless 'cubic' is explicitly stated. The text says 'single crystalline structures'. I will not infer 'cubic' without explicit text. \n\n5. **Construct Records**: \n   - **Record 1**: Si-dots, peroxidase, TMB varied. Km=1.502, Vmax=14.72. Fixed H2O2=20 mM. \n   - **Record 2**: Si-dots, peroxidase, H2O2 varied. Km=0.065, Vmax=5.65. Fixed TMB=0.32 mM. \n\n6. **Refinement**: \n   - `ccat_value`: Not available (stock concentration missing). \n   - `c_min`/`c_max`: Not available (ranges not specified in text). \n   - `temperature`: 40 (inferred from optimization context, but strictly speaking, the kinetic sentence doesn't specify. However, the optimization paragraph concludes 40°C is best, and kinetics are usually done at optimal. I will include 40). \n   - `ph`: 4.0. \n   - `formula`: Si. \n   - `length`: 12 (average). \n   - `width`: 12. \n   - `depth`: 12. \n   - `vmax_unit`: 10^-8 M s^-1. \n   - `km_unit`: mM. \n\nLet's double check the temperature. The text says 'The experimental data imply that the Si-dots reached their highest catalytic activity at the vicinity of pH 4.0 and 40 °C.' Then 'To investigate the kinetic mechanism...'. It is standard practice to perform kinetics at optimal conditions. I will use 40. \n\nWait, the text says 'Kinetic experiments were carried out using 10 μL of Si-dots in 0.5 mL of 0.2 M NaAc–HAc buffer solution (pH 4.0) containing 320 μM TMB as the substrate, and the H2O2 concentration was 20 mM.' This sentence seems to desc